\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\lang1040\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. With broken heart and contrite sigh,
\par A trembling sinner, Lord, I cry;
\par Thy pardoning grace is rich and free:
\par O God, be merciful to me!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. I smite upon my troubled breast,
\par With deep and conscious guilt oppressed;
\par Christ and His cross my only plea:
\par O God, be merciful to me!
\par \pard\tx1500\tab 
\par \pard\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Far off I stand with tearful eyes,
\par Nor dare uplift them to the skies;
\par But Thou dost all my anguish see:
\par O God, be merciful to me!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Nor alms, nor deeds that I have done,
\par Can for a single sin atone;
\par To Calvary alon I flee:
\par O God, be merciful to me!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. And when, redeemed from sin and hell,
\par With all the ransomed throng I dwell,
\par My raptured song shall ever be:
\par God has been merciful to me! 
\par \lang1033\f1 
\par \cf1\lang1040\ul\b\f2 
\par }

